cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use roomshift, please cite it as below."
title: "roomshift: cross-room adaptation of mmWave radar and Wi-Fi human pose estimation"
abstract: >-
  3-D human pose from mmWave radar or Wi-Fi CSI degrades in a new room. On the four rooms of MM-Fi, held out in
  turn and streamed frame by frame, roomshift decomposes the cross-room error into the person's position and the
  body's shape, tests whether the radar-to-pose transform differs between rooms with each subject's position held
  fixed, shows why label-free test-time adaptation of normalization statistics destroys absolute pose, and compares
  a gradient-free 12-parameter output correction from sparse labels with tuned online fine-tuning across label
  budgets, including a correction fitted once per room. Tests pin every reported number to the released results.
type: software
